<title>USA: Ancor, Nippon Telephone to develop device.</title>
<headline>Ancor, Nippon Telephone to develop device.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ancor Communications Inc, Nippon Telephone and Telegraph Corp and Hucom Inc, the distributor of Ancor Fibre Channel products in Japan, said Friday they agreed to design and market a high speed data transmission technology.</p>
<p>Plans call for development of a Fibre Channel that would allow data to move smoothly from ATM (asynchronous transfer mode) to STM (synchronous transfer mode).</p>
<p>Fibre Channel is a high-speed data communications technology that provides gigabit-per-second transmission rates in local and metropolitan area networks.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
